{"file":{"content":"Wielandt's equality theorem this is the assertion that\n$\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi})<\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\mathbf1})$ for all $\\chi\\notin\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$;\nit reduces to showing the principal-unit functional equation\n$\\psi(3a+1)=\\psi(a^2)$ on $C=1+3\\Z/3^r$ has no nontrivial solution (it already\nfails at $r=2$). Verified numerically over the full character group for\n$Q\\le3^4$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Conductor monotonicity]\\label{conj:mono}\nAmong non-coboundary sectors, the maximal gap ratio occurs at conductor $9$.\nVerified numerically for $Q\\le3^5$ and $s\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{corollary}[Conditional constant gap]\\label{cor:const}\nAssume \\cref{conj:nocob,conj:mono}. Then for all $Q=3^r$ ($r\\ge2$) and\n$s\\in[0,1]$,\n\\[\n\\rho(\\Lcal^{\\mathrm{sync}}_{s,Q,\\chi})\\le(1-\\kappa_0)\\,\n\\rho(\\Lcal^{\\mathrm{sync}}_{s,Q,\\mathbf1}),\n\\qquad \\chi\\notin\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle,\n\\]\nwith $\\kappa_0=1-0.9069\\approx0.0931$ the gap of the fixed conductor-$9$ operator.\nIn particular $\\kappa_Q^{\\mathrm{sync}/\\mathrm{cob}}\\ge\\kappa_0>0$, stronger than\nthe fall-back target $\\kappa_Q\\gg1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\nBy \\cref{prop:cond} each conductor-$3^c$ sector's ratio is $r$-independent; by\n\\cref{conj:mono} the maximum over non-coboundary sectors is attained at conductor\n$9$, whose operator is fixed and has ratio $0.9069$; by \\cref{conj:nocob} there\nare no other zero-gap sectors. The bound holds for every non-coboundary $\\chi$\nuniformly in $r$.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\paragraph{Proof program for \\cref{conj:mono}.} The natural route is\nDoeblin/block minorisation by \\emph{principal-unit cancellation}: for each\nnon-coboundary $\\chi$, exhibit from every bulk state a finite admissible block\nfamily carrying untwisted mass $\\ge\\alpha$ on which\n$\\lvert\\E[\\chi(\\text{endpoint})]\\rvert\\le1-\\eta$. Where the block images contain a\nfull coset of a subgroup $H$ with $\\chi|_H\\ne1$, cancellation is exact\n($\\sum_{u\\in H}\\chi(uh)=0$)---the likely source of the observed flat, conductor-\nmonotone gap. A height/QSD transfer step (the synchronized weights on paired\nblocks are comparable, $w_s(w_1)/w_s(w_2)\\in[C^{-1},C]$ uniformly for\n$s\\in[0,1]$, and the blocks remain in the QSD bulk up to $O(e^{-cL})$) carries the\nresidue cancellation into the killed sync operator.\n\n\\section*{Conclusion}\n\\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Conclusion}\n\nThe defect cocycle relocates rather than removes the difficulty. The\nreorganisations of known structure are in hand---the sliding-window congruence,\nthe annealed Fourier gap, and (the new rigorous core) the proof that the\nquadratic character is valuation parity in disguise, hence an exact coboundary.\nThis forces the correct statement of the finite spectral hypothesis: a gap for\nall \\emph{non-coboundary} characters of the faithful synchronized operator,\nrelative to the valuation-pushforward residue reference. On that quotient the gap\nis observed to be constant and conductor-controlled, and the remaining\nfinite-operator task is the precise pair \\cref{conj:nocob,conj:mono} (no further\ncoboundaries; conductor monotonicity / principal-unit cancellation). The genuinely\nquenched arrow---bad orbit $\\Rightarrow$ finite non-coboundary spectral shadow---\nremains the open keystone.","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","numLines":60,"startLine":610,"totalLines":677},"type":"text"}